<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech CSU raises 1996 sugar beet harvest forecast.</title>
<headline>Czech CSU raises 1996 sugar beet harvest forecast.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Tuesday it had revised its 1996 sugar beet harvest forecast to 4.38 million tonnes, up 1.4 percent from its September estimate and 18 percent above the 1995 harvest.</p>
<p>The CSU said that based on its survey completed on October 15, yield per hectare would reach 42.06 tonnes, up from the earlier estimate of 41.46 tonnes.</p>
<p>Local experts said in late summer that sugar production this year would exceed 500,000 tonnes, up from 460,035 tonnes in 1995, allowing some exports. But they warned at the beginning of October that bad weather was hampering the harvest.</p>
<p>				1996	     1996		1995</p>
<p>				Oct forecast   Sept forecast</p>
<p> Beet harvest (tonnes)  4,379,089	4,317,079	 3,711,602</p>
<p> Yield/hectare		  42.06	    41.46	     39.86</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
